    "rationale": "Cohen syndrome uniquely ties together the retinal dystrophy with intellectual disability, microcephaly, truncal obesity, joint hyperextensibility, and transient childhood neutropenia. Bardet-Biedl is less fitting because these particular hematologic and dysmorphic features are not its hallmarks. Alström does not explain the microcephaly, neutropenia, and joint hypermobility.",
